# Business Rules

## One note per session

A session owns exactly one revision note.

```
Session

↓

Revision Note
```

Unique index on

```
sessionId
```

enforces this.

---

## Empty note deletion

Saving an empty summary deletes the note automatically.

---

## Attachment ownership

Attachments belong to sessions.

Deleting a session automatically removes

* note
* attachments

through Room cascade rules.

---

## Local image storage

Gallery images are copied into Omega private storage.

The original gallery path is not stored.

Only Omega's internal path is persisted.

---

# Architecture Decisions

## Why notes belong to sessions

Because sessions represent actual learning events.

A note answers

"What was learned during this work session?"

not

"What do I know about this topic?"

---

## Why attachments do not reference notes

One session has one note.

Adding another foreign key

```
Attachment

↓

Note
```

would duplicate information.

Session already provides the relationship.

---

## Why notes are independent of revision

Notes are historical records.

They never change after learning except user edits.

Revision tracking is a separate concern.

---

# Planned Revision Feature

The current implementation provides only learning history.

The actual revision engine will be implemented separately.

A new entity is planned.

```
RevisionStateEntity
```

Its responsibility is

* last revised time
* revision count
* future scheduling
* confidence
* memory strength
* AI summary
* spaced repetition

It will **not** duplicate note content.

---

# Planned Revision Architecture

```
Project

↓

Node

↓

